{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e","id":1552856,"title":"Question about Yozis and charms 2e / 3e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-03T10:54:00-07:00","id":1552856,"title":"Question about Yozis and charms 2e / 3e","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Totally new to exalted, so if this is clearly stated anywhere, or if any misconceptions there, please correct me:<br /> <br /> <br /> I understand that the Yozis are defined by their charms, that in a sense they are the charms. Also, that every Yozi learns the charms that their exalted learn.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>IF so, then aren't the Yozis crosscontaminating each other when their exalted learn charms from a different Yozi?</li> <li>Isn't the Ebon Dragon becoming more a more different as the Fiends learn charms from other creatures?</li> <li>Are Devil-Tigers also defined by the charms they know?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T12:38:54-07:00","id":1552857,"title":"","content":"1. Think of the 2e Yozis as Charm trees. Malfeas <i>is</i> the set of Malfeas Charms, everything that defines him is in there and everything in there defines him. An Infernal Exalted who creates a new Malfeas Charm is adding to the definition of Malfeas, within the confines of Malfeas's preexisting definition (you can't make a Malfeas Charm that makes him <i>less</i> like what Malfeas already is). A Slayer who learns an Ebon Dragon Charm is not turning it into a Malfeas Charm, he just has Charms from multiple Yozis. Malfeas remains the same.<br /> <br /> 2. In the same manner, Fiends aren't transforming foreign Charms into Ebon Dragon Charms. They know Ebon Dragon Charms, and they also know these Spirit Charms or whatever. The Ebon Dragon is only transformed by adding new Charms branching out of his Charm tree.<br /> <br /> 3. The short answer is no. Infernal Exalted who've developed the Devil-Tiger/Rising Phoenix magic aren't Primordials (Yozis being a subset of Primordials). There's an actual human there, underneath all those Permanent Charms, with a Motivation of his own and a soul of his own. His self-definition comes from being a person and he retains all of the free will and capacity for self-contradiction and complicated feelings that any person has, minus whatever constraints are imposed on him by individual weird Permanent Charms he knows. To the extent that he has become like a Yozi, he is only like a Yozi in the specific ways his Charms (such as the Devil-Tiger tree) have made him like one, and not any other ways.<br /> <br /> This means that if, say, Chwen Screaming-Curses makes the Chwen Screaming-Curses Infernal Charm tree through Devil-Tiger/Rising Phoenix, and then teaches a Chwen Screaming-Curses Charm to another Infernal, and that other Infernal invents a new Chwen Screaming-Curses Charm, Chwen Screaming-Curses, who is an actual specific human, does not automatically learn that new Charm. Because the Chwen Screaming-Curses tree is a tree of Infernal Charms, though, it <i>is</i> likely to have a bunch of transformative Permanent Charms in it that will start to limit the nature of Chwen Screaming-Curses, the person, if he invents and learns them. That's just what Infernal Charm trees are like: they start with a few core thematic elements and build outward from there through thematic associations, often including a lot of Charms that transform what you are like and may limit the things you do in exchange for power, which you may have to route through as prerequisites to get to other Charms you might want. The Chwen Screaming-Curses tree, whatever form it takes, cannot escape following this model.<br /> <br /> Here's the long answer getting into the unnecessary weeds:<br /> <br /> When we say Malfeas is the set of Malfeas Charms, we mean that the Yozi Malfeas who exists as the Demon City is an entity that knows the full set of Malfeas Charms, that probably came fully-formed from the Wyld at the dawn of the birth of the Primordials (though back then he wasn't Malfeas yet, fetich-death transformed who he is and what his Charms are). At the very top of the Malfeas Charm tree is an Essence 10 Charm called Malfeas Cosmic Principle. Learning this Malfeas Charm effectively <i>makes you the Yozi Malfeas.</i> If an Infernal Exalt learned so many Malfeas Charms and gathered so much Essence that he was able to learn Malfeas Cosmic Principle, he would cease to be an Exalted human being and instead become a Yozi. Since Yozis can only know their own Charms, he would lose all of his non-Malfeas Charms. Any unique properties of the Yozis as beings, like instantly learning all the Charms added to your tree, being able to adapt the Charms of foreign Yozis as Charms of your own tree, or so on, are conferred either by this Charm or by other very high level Malfeas Charms branching out from there. The other Yozis have corresponding Charms at the top of their trees.<br /> <br /> Yes, this does mean that if a Slayer learned Malfeas Cosmic Principle, there would then be two Malfeases, the one that was birthed from the Wyld long ago and underwent fetich death, and the newborn Malfeas who used to be a Slayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T13:08:09-07:00","id":1552858,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I just noticed the title is 2e / 3e:<br /> <br /> Expect little to none of this to apply to Third Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T15:43:49-07:00","id":1552860,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> thanks for the very, very detailed explanation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Further questions then:<br /> <br /> 4. What happens with the Exalted Spark when undergoing Devil-Tiger transformation?<br /> <br /> 5. Can a Devil-Tiger create their own [Person-name] Cosmic Principle charm?<br /> <br /> 6. Becoming Devil-Tiger would allow an Infernal exalted to change or lose the Anima Banner, Anima Effect and Caste Abilities that they had? So a Defiler picking some Caste Abilities of a Malefactor and the Anima Effect of the Fiend for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-03-2025, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T19:34:09-07:00","id":1552861,"title":"","content":"4. Stays with you. Becoming a Devil Tiger is kind of being a half-Yozi/half-Exalt.<br /> <br /> 5. Yes, but explicitly cannot learn it. That only becomes an option for the next incarnation of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> 6. Yes, or could have an entirely new Anima power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T20:28:39-07:00","id":1552862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552861#post1552861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Stays with you. Becoming a Devil Tiger is kind of being a half-Yozi/half-Exalt.<br /> <br /> 5. Yes, but explicitly cannot learn it. That only becomes an option for the next incarnation of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> 6. Yes, or could have an entirely new Anima power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, if I get this correctly and please fix my example when it gets wrong:<ul><li><b>lbeaumanior </b>is a Fiend and he becomes a Devil-Tiger.</li> <li>He decides to gain new Caste Abilities (some of the Defilers and some of the Malefactors because of reasons).</li> <li>He creates <b>lbeaumanior Cosmic Principle</b> charm (but somehow can not learn it even if he creates it?).</li> <li>Then he is killed and his Exaltation goes to <b>Yue Ryong</b>, who has the Anima power of Fiends but five among the Caste abilities of the Defilers and Malefactors.</li> <li>Eventually <b>Yue Ryong</b> gets to be powerful enough to qualify for <b>lbeaumanior Cosmic Principle</b> and they become the Yozi <b>lbeaumanior</b>.</li> <li>Optionally, <b>Yue Ryong</b> can become a Devil-Tiger on their own, modifying the Exaltation again, and creating their own <b>Yue Ryong</b>\u200b\u200b<b> Cosmic Principle</b> charm.\u200b</li> <li>If <b>lbeaumanior </b>\u200bwas never killed, he would have been an immortal (or mortal perhaps?) half-Yozi half-Exalted creature as described in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>'s post.</li> </ul>Did I get all that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-06-2025, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T20:35:29-07:00","id":1552863,"title":"","content":"Looks basically correct - although, as a generic Yozi charm, <b>lbeaumanior Cosmic Principle</b> is created effectively automatically by creating the charmset to begin with. This whole process does take approximately 1000 years for the next generation to do, but thankfully the Infernal's Essence-rating-restricted lifespan does <i>heavily</i> incentivise them to get into a position of at least contemplating it.<br /> <br /> Edit: It is also worth noting that the Yozi lbeaumanior isn't strictly the same as the Exalt lbeaumanior - they are a vision of lbeaumanior flattened and widened by the process of becoming a thematic statement akin to a Yozi. The Exalt lbeaumanior presumably did not start out having the charms of 'gain benefits when acting like lbeaumanior did in this one specific instance' and 'make it functionally impossible to do the thing that lbeaumanior hated doing'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","user":"Yue Ryong","date":".  Expanded the point slightly. 08-03-2025, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T22:54:49-07:00","id":1552870,"title":"","content":"I would say basically the same thing Yue Ryong said, but phrase it differently: (Yozi) Cosmic Principle isn't really a Charm that is &quot;invented.&quot; Once an Infernal Charm tree exists, the potential for (Yozi) Cosmic Principle already exists, and it is just a matter of somebody eventually getting around to learning it.<br /> <br /> So Ibeaumanior does not create Ibeaumanior Cosmic Principle. It's not a Charm anybody knows, because Ibeaumanior, as a Devil-Tiger, can't learn it, and nobody else has access to learning it. If Ibeaumanior dies and Yue Ryong inherits his Exaltation with his Ibeaumanior Caste, Yue Ryong can hypothetically eventually learn Ibeaumanior Cosmic Principle. So: who created or invented Ibeaumanior Cosmic Principle? Not really anybody, except in the sense that Ibeaumanior created the Charm tree. But Yue Ryong is the first person to ever manifest and learn it. And now he's not a person, now he's the exaggerated image of Ibeaumanior as viewed through the essentialist, transformative lens of Infernal magic.<br /> <br /> I'd also object to calling Devil-Tiger Infernals &quot;half-Exalted, half-Yozi.&quot; They're not true Yozis, and they're not any less Exalted than they were before. They're Infernal Exalted who have a subset of Yozi-like qualities.<br /> <br /> It's just that what an Infernal Exalted can be turns out to encompass some really weird possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T11:56:03-07:00","id":1552884,"title":"","content":"Thanks to both of you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar955_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"955\" data-vbnamecard=\"955\">Yue Ryong</a> for your replies.<br /> <br /> Final question (I think), are Devil-Tigers, immortals? As in no: maximum lifespan and unageing. Or is there a charm somewhere that they could learn to get that result? Like using the Fiend ability or Sorcery to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T12:00:58-07:00","id":1552885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552884#post1552884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks to both of you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar955_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"955\" data-vbnamecard=\"955\">Yue Ryong</a> for your replies.<br /> <br /> Final question (I think), are Devil-Tigers, immortals? As in no: maximum lifespan and unageing. Or is there a charm somewhere that they could learn to get that result? Like using the Fiend ability or Sorcery to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It's about the first thing that the Triumphant Howl of the Devil-Tiger says it gives you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T09:24:26-07:00","id":1552952,"title":"","content":"If someone, devil-tiger or otherwise, learns<b> a [Yozi] Cosmic Principle</b> charm, what happens with the Exaltation Spark?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar955_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"955\" data-vbnamecard=\"955\">Yue Ryong</a> sorry to keep tagging you, but you are the ones who have replied already, and seem to be in agreement with each other's arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T10:21:57-07:00","id":1552954,"title":"","content":"It passes on.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If an Exalt, his Exaltation departs as it no longer recognizes him as human, leaving him with \u201conly\u201d the Primordial power he has become. </div> </div> </div>Given that this is the same charm that gives you a 1000m essence pool, this feels like an... acceptable trade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T19:53:46-07:00","id":1552965,"title":"","content":"A devil-tiger (as in somebody who knows Triumphant Howl) can't learn (Yozi) Cosmic Principle. I assume you mean &quot;the inheritor of a devil-tiger's custom caste.&quot;<br /> The Infernal Exaltation moves on from an Infernal who learns (Yozi) Cosmic Principle in the same way that it would move on if the Infernal instead died.<br /> <br /> There <i>are,</i> mind you, some trade-offs to becoming a Primordial. All your perfect defenses gain a Greater Imperfection on top of their normal Imperfection. You lose access to all Charms outside of your Primordial Charm tree (so becoming the artificial Yozi Ibeaumanior means you can only learn Ibeaumanior Charms, etc, and say, if you know any Malfeas Charms or Adorjan Charms, you lose them). Primordial Charm trees all deliberately have blind spots and situations they just aren't well prepared for.<br /> <br /> More trade-offs await if you go further into the Primordial transfiguration. For instance, (Yozi) Glory Incarnate, which gives you big Primordial dice pools and Primordial-grade Shaping defenses, also severely cripples your ability to act outside the confines of your personal Excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T13:04:49-07:00","id":1552987,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm inclined to say that an Infernal who has developed the powers branching from Triumphant Howl of the Devil Tiger will not have any Cosmic Principle Charm that the successors of their Caste could learn.<br /> <br /> Partially because I don't think it makes sense given how there's no plausible Primordial form for them to be transformed into, and partially because I think the narrative trajectory of it is all off. The power to develop a new Excellency and redevelop Caste and all that is a stand for oneself as Exalted against the form of transcendence that being able to transform into a Yozi entails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T13:06:40-07:00","id":1552988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552965#post1552965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordial Charm trees all deliberately have blind spots and situations they just aren't well prepared for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't the manual have some line about how all the Yozis have at least some versions of the Charms of other Yozis, modified to fit in their own cascades, but that Infernals couldn't learn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T14:52:53-07:00","id":1552990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552988#post1552988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't the manual have some line about how all the Yozis have at least some versions of the Charms of other Yozis, modified to fit in their own cascades, but that Infernals couldn't learn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But not, like, <i>any</i> other Yozi Charms they want. I took that as more of a design decision that &quot;I'm not writing six different variations of the wyldshaping/hellshaping Charm, just say that one can be reskinned.&quot;<br /> <br /> The modifications presumably also work to preserve the Yozis' conceptual blind spots.<br /> <br /> You're not going to have an Ebon Dragon Charm to be very earnestly convincing and cooperative, is what I'm saying. You can do it through a weird end run by way of transforming into other people, but you have to do a weird end run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T15:10:33-07:00","id":1552991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552990#post1552990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not going to have an Ebon Dragon Charm to be very earnestly convincing and cooperative, is what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Second Edition gave Infernals any Charms to do that.<br /> <br /> But that's splitting hairs. <i>My</i> perspective on that line was that it was intended to reconcile the mechanical underpinnings of a Charm set for the Infernal Exalted (and the premise that they were utilising the actual powers of the Yozis) with a necessity that, in the event that an actual Yozi ever became an antagonist in a game, that their capabilities should be somewhat more well rounded.<br /> <br /> Still, I'll admit that it's a difficult thing to figure out. I'm of the opinion that the whole approach bit off more than it could chew in several respects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T16:27:52-07:00","id":1552992,"title":"","content":"In short Kimberry doesn't have that one (was it Malfean or Cecelyne) charm that causes an eruption of sand under a target to shred them because that's not Kimberry. On the hand no one is arguing much if the sea that marched against flame can murder people by willing murder geysers to exist and go off under a person. <br /> <br /> A fully ascended Devil Tiger is going to have a lot of room where they can function, same as the Yozi and the Primordial before them. The limitations are likely to be more noticeable from an exterior perspective than an interior one. Basically my thinking Malfeas isn't indirect or big on catspaw tactics not because the first excellency of Malfeas prevents him from acting in subterfuge, but because Malfeas is direct by dint of his role as king and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T22:15:51-07:00","id":1552999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552992#post1552992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short Kimberry doesn't have that one (was it Malfean or Cecelyne) charm that causes an eruption of sand under a target to shred them because that's not Kimberry. On the hand no one is arguing much if the sea that marched against flame can murder people by willing murder geysers to exist and go off under a person.<br /> <br /> A fully ascended Devil Tiger is going to have a lot of room where they can function, same as the Yozi and the Primordial before them. The limitations are likely to be more noticeable from an exterior perspective than an interior one. Basically my thinking Malfeas isn't indirect or big on catspaw tactics not because the first excellency of Malfeas prevents him from acting in subterfuge, but because Malfeas is direct by dint of his role as king and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Flanderization. Rendering a deeply ashamed titan who can't break free and subsequently plots the most cruelly among the Yozis to hurt Creation and the gods into a screaming, one-note killcrazy since 2009.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T23:29:27-07:00","id":1553001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552999#post1552999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, Flanderization. Rendering a deeply ashamed titan who can't break free and subsequently plots the most cruelly among the Yozis to hurt Creation and the gods into a screaming, one-note killcrazy since 2009.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you want to view it, not what I said though and we are talking about 2e afterall.<br /> I'm saying people are who they are. A devil tiger going full ascendant isn't going to suddenly notice &quot;Oh I have restrictions on my thoughts and how I can act. Must be because I'm not human.&quot; Its just becoming themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-01T06:37:52-08:00","id":1558055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552965#post1552965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A devil-tiger (as in somebody who knows Triumphant Howl) can't learn (Yozi) Cosmic Principle. I assume you mean &quot;the inheritor of a devil-tiger's custom caste.&quot;<br /> The Infernal Exaltation moves on from an Infernal who learns (Yozi) Cosmic Principle in the same way that it would move on if the Infernal instead died.<br /> <br /> There <i>are,</i> mind you, some trade-offs to becoming a Primordial. All your perfect defenses gain a Greater Imperfection on top of their normal Imperfection. You lose access to all Charms outside of your Primordial Charm tree (so becoming the artificial Yozi Ibeaumanior means you can only learn Ibeaumanior Charms, etc, and say, if you know any Malfeas Charms or Adorjan Charms, you lose them). Primordial Charm trees all deliberately have blind spots and situations they just aren't well prepared for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dare say the Ibeaumanior neo-Yozi <b>might</b> manifest/develop charms of its own that somewhat mimic the capacities of the lost Malfeas or Adorjan Charms, since something such as a Yozi tend to not take well to the idea of loss of capacity and limitations that come from outside its own self.<br /> <br /> Though that would depend on how much Ibeaumanior identifies whatever they did as <i>its </i>capacities instead of curious tricks of the &quot;intermediary step in its transcedence&quot; that was the devil-tiger Yue Ryong - and either way these &quot;new&quot; charms will reinterpreted through the lens of themes, vices &amp; blindspots that define Ibeaumanior the neo-Yozi, what could go from &quot;light coat of hell-paint in another shade&quot; to &quot;almost completely different charm that does happen to share a few functionalities, kind of&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T08:57:56-07:00","id":1559602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1552856-question-about-yozis-and-charms-2e-3e?p=1552862#post1552862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, if I get this correctly and please fix my example when it gets wrong:<ul><li><b>lbeaumanior </b>is a Fiend and he becomes a Devil-Tiger.</li> <li>He decides to gain new Caste Abilities (some of the Defilers and some of the Malefactors because of reasons).</li> <li>He creates <b>lbeaumanior Cosmic Principle</b> charm (but somehow can not learn it even if he creates it?).</li> <li>Then he is killed and his Exaltation goes to <b>Yue Ryong</b>, who has the Anima power of Fiends but five among the Caste abilities of the Defilers and Malefactors.</li> <li>Eventually <b>Yue Ryong</b> gets to be powerful enough to qualify for <b>lbeaumanior Cosmic Principle</b> and they become the Yozi <b>lbeaumanior</b>.</li> <li>Optionally, <b>Yue Ryong</b> can become a Devil-Tiger on their own, modifying the Exaltation again, and creating their own <b>Yue Ryong</b><b> Cosmic Principle</b> charm.\u200b</li> <li>If <b>lbeaumanior </b>\u200bwas never killed, he would have been an immortal (or mortal perhaps?) half-Yozi half-Exalted creature as described in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>'s post.</li> </ul>Did I get all that right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A bit of necromancy, but appropiated to the topic here.<br /> <br /> For lbeaumanior the exalt that dies and whose exaltation goes to Yue Ryong, are there any specific benefits, limitations, or anything at all happening with his ghost? Does he gain or lose something by having been a Devil-Tiger? Or when the lbeaumanior Yozi manifests?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar955_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"955\" data-vbnamecard=\"955\">Yue Ryong</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> I appreciate your comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T11:41:39-07:00","id":1559606,"title":"","content":"Ghosts in general don't get much out of being former Exalts outside of starting at higher Essence and retaining generic abilities like Martial Arts or Sorcery. Given how extensive the changes they've made to their soul already are, it's <b>probably</b> difficult to make any assumptions about how Devil-Tiger ghosts differ from that baseline; there's no clear canon material that indicates what to expect, at least. The closest equivalent (the emergence of Hekatoncheires from the lower souls of the Neverborn) might be informative, but the differences are sufficient to caution against over-reading.<br /> <br /> I <i>wouldn't</i> expect Ghost!lbeaumanior to get any additional benefits if/when Yozi!lbeaumanior emerges, beyond possibly some extra cred in the underworld and people wanting to grab them for theoretical arcane links to exploit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T23:16:48-07:00","id":1559613,"title":"","content":"The dead ghost of a Devil-Tiger Infernal Exalted is simply the dead ghost of an Exalted. The ghost may have an unusual appearance to match any unusual appearance her Charms gave her in life, but she is probably not meaningfully different from other ghosts of powerful Exalted, given that Infernal magic is generally established to play poorly, when it plays at all, with necromantic Essence. She is not privileged in any particular way by the rise of her successor Yozi, except for having firsthand knowledge of what being Ibeaumanior is like, and what directions her magic had been taking that transformation in life. The utility of this knowledge is dubious.<br /> <br /> In general, the experience of being a ghost witnessing somebody else incarnate the legend of your magical persona is likely one of frustrated impotence, and the ghost will probably be better off the more they're able to separate from their former persona and pursue their own goals now as a ghost \u2014 something they will likely find quite difficult, between the ghostly tendency to stagnate and calcify personal traits from life, and the monomaniacal, compulsive nature of Infernal personas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}